{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"gibbs-comparison","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618","passage_ref":"sha256:fa472c25832b36a2061f212196277009f716c230a658520bb4b4f2ed8173d74b/papers/long.md/sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json/passages/gibbs-comparison","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","span":{"end_byte":223136,"end_line":4910,"start_byte":221223,"start_line":4869},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&ref=sha256%3A47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Ordinary derivation in this authored edition, not an attribution of the whole synthesis to a cited external paper. The log-sum and entropy identities give the deterministic bounds; Gaussian concentration uses Lipschitz constant sqrt((n-1)/(2n^2)); counting configurations gives the conditional tail. Exact Gibbs sampling is a distributional premise, not an efficient sampling algorithm. The Born law and QAOA angle construction are distinct. No Lean or Comparator coverage and no complete formal dependency audit are asserted.","citation_ids":["authored_gibbs_comparison","scalar-r2-26-cite-parisi-formula"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"Finite Gibbs values and exact Gibbs samples","locator":"papers/qaoa-sk/long/reasoning-record.md §11.1.2, passage:gibbs-comparison; content-addressed source edition, not an external-paper attribution.","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For the pure zero-field SK Hamiltonian and beta>0, let L_n=max_sigma H_n(sigma)/n, F_n,beta=(n beta)^(-1)log sum_sigma exp(beta H_n(sigma)), and U_n,beta be the exact Gibbs mean energy per spin. For each instance, 0<=F_n,beta-L_n<=log(2)/beta and 0<=L_n-U_n,beta<=log(2)/beta. For n>=2 and s>0, P_J(|L_n-E L_n|>s)<=2 exp(-n^2 s^2/(n-1)). For an exact Gibbs draw Sigma, P(H_n(Sigma)/n<=L_n-s | J)<=min(1,exp(n(log(2)-beta s))). Since E L_n tends to P_*, both value expectations tend to P_* along every joint n→infinity,beta→infinity; an exact Gibbs draw tends to P_* in the joint disorder-and-sampling probability.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.parisi_formula"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"field:63cd5e58d26cf30b3c192b423245ba74e3d22c5311f8f328d210625889d2be9e","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/sources/authored_long_comparisons_20261024"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"field:8c201f5a593d2d82e1b5b0c2a92a488d6e3b54a3d08856361b7c0f2cc8257e46","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/citations/authored_gibbs_comparison"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"field:8f4393649e33a60f843cb906758697a48cb1268e42ee64f5bdf8a12cbb055862","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993e